cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use CrashDefNet, please cite it as below."
title: "CrashDefNet: Learned Deformation Prediction on Simulation Meshes"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Stocker
    given-names: Felix
    email: felix.stocker@sto-eng.de
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-24"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/stofe94/crash-def-net"
abstract: >-
  CrashDefNet is a deep-learning tool for predicting structural deformation from
  finite element simulations. It covers the chain from raw simulation data to the
  predicted deformation and implements MeshGraphNet and the
  MeshGraphNet-Transformer (MGN-T) in one pipeline, evaluated with the metrics of
  the MGN-T paper on DeepMind's deforming_plate benchmark.
keywords:
  - graph neural networks
  - MeshGraphNet
  - MeshGraphNet-Transformer
  - crash simulation
  - CAE
  - finite element method
  - surrogate model
references:
